From a598e7a060623050686a06ed259df97fdef4728f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:08:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 69/97] qsa: start the clip-counter reader after capture, not
 on the first forward

The FP8 KV clip counter's reader thread used to start on the first eager forward, before CUDA graph capture, so
its device-to-host copies could overlap a capture. _qsa_clip_count now only allocates the per-layer counter; the
reader is started by a hook that guard_telemetry runs after warmup and capture (or at once if capture is already
done). Counting is unchanged. Tests cover the order, idempotence and a failing control that restores the old start.
---
